1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,190
This is an urgent announcement
about the upcoming City-Wide

3
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,630
Autumn Yo-Yo Tournament.

4
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,070
Chengnan High School will be there too.

5
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,990
They're our old Rivals.

6
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:41,310
I'll definitely be back!

7
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,220
The majority of the funding and the Training Facilities

8
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:46,500
you'll have to figure that out yourselves.

9
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,470
How are we supposed to do that?

10
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:52,830
Because even Coach Tony is scared of her big mouth.

11
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:58,150
Stop right there!

12
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Episode 2

13
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,300
If you keep pushing me...

14
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:08,220
I won't be so nice!

15
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,660
Put it down! Put it down!

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,460
Stay back! Don't come any closer!

17
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,860
What are you doing? Put that down!

18
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:32,530
Look! That's my wallet right there.

19
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,780
Grab him! Stop him!

20
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,500
Now that's a true Yo-Yo Master.

21
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:52,080
That "Flying Leaf" move he just did...

22
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,400
it's evolved from the basic fundamentals.

23
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,580
If we had someone like him on our Team...

24
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,580
then the Championship

25
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:02,460
would definitely belong to the Jianghai Team.

26
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:30,780
Popcorn, is your info legit?

27
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,660
If you don't believe me, why'd you even come?

28
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,580
The hardest thing to endure in life...

29
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,980
is not being trusted. Got it?

30
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,900
Understood.

31
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,340
Coach Tony's acting so weird.

32
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,700
If this is such great news, why didn't he tell us sooner?

33
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,590
If we'd known earlier, we could've
started preparing ages ago.

34
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,580
Exactly.

35
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:57,180
Who leaked it?

36
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,700
It's gotta be Mickey.

37
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,620
He's totally unreliable.

38
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,180
What are we gonna do?

39
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:22,620
I still haven't secured the funding.

40
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:36,030
Without any funding right now...

41
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,980
we can't get anything done.

42
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,460
Coach Tony, open up!

43
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:51,900
There's no hiding from this.

44
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,140
Attention!

45
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:00,990
I hereby announce...

46
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,940
The day after tomorrow, we will hold a School-wide tryout

47
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:06,780
to form the Official Jianghai High
School Yo-Yo Team— The Jianghai Team.

48
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:09,180
Everyone go home and start practicing hard.

49
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:12,060
Spots are limited. Don't miss your shot.

50
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:13,980
Alright, dismissed.

51
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:19,260
Yeah!

52
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,040
Hmph, I was nice enough to tell them,

53
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,500
and I didn't even get a "thank you."

54
00:05:58,200 --> 00:06:00,060
If your Eastern Intuition...

55
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,940
can't surpass my Western Speed...

56
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:07,740
then you'll never be able to beat me.

57
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,580
In a way...

58
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:17,820
second place is just another name for a loser.

59
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,340
Old Li, that move's still not smooth.

60
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,260
Maybe try practicing a different one.

61
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,180
I've gotta learn it eventually.

62
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,400
I can't just run away every time something gets hard.

63
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,540
Disconnected number again.

64
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,380
Hello? Is this Zhang Lu?

65
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,300
Zhang Lu!

66
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,740
It really is you, old classmate!

67
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,620
Oh, so should I be calling you "Boss Zhang" now?

68
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,420
It's me, Tony!

69
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,260
The Tony who used to sleep in the bunk above you!

70
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:10,620
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

71
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,980
You used to call me Little Tony,

72
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:15,900
but I changed my name, remember?

73
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,300
Old friend...

74
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,220
I need a favor.

75
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,980
Sorry! Sorry!

76
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,380
Hey, Tony!

77
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,740
I can't believe you've got gray hair now, too.

78
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:57,660
Talk about a small world.

79
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,020
Of all the cars in the World, it had to be hers.

80
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,380
It's you.

81
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,260
This is your car?

82
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,700
Of course it's my car.

83
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:10,620
Right.

84
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,500
Where are you headed? I'll give you a ride.

85
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:17,340
No, no, I... I like to walk.

86
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:20,220
Just taking a stroll. See you around!

87
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:21,660
Hey, Tony!

88
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,540
Get in. I need to talk to you.

89
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,340
Why not?

90
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,220
You haven't changed a bit over the years.

91
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:36,060
I used to consider you my Ultimate Rival.

92
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:37,810
Guess I was wrong.

93
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:41,820
What Ultimate Rival?

94
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,220
The Yo-Yo Tournament, obviously!

95
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:48,540
I heard you're coaching the Jianghai High School Team now.

96
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:53,340
What are you spacing out for?

97
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,220
Oh, you're talking about the Tournament.

98
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,160
I don't see you as a rival at all.

99
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:00,540
Honestly...

100
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,900
a worthy rival for our Jianghai Team
hasn't even been born yet.

101
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,300
Tony, all these years and you haven't changed a bit.

102
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:07,740
Still all talk.

103
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:11,580
What "all talk"? I'm just stating the obvious.

104
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,460
What "obvious"?

105
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:17,340
The Tournament hasn't even started yet this year.

106
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:20,220
Let's let the facts speak for themselves, alright?

107
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:24,060
Men like you... no wonder...

108
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,390
No wonder what?

109
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:29,790
Spit it out.

110
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,260
No wonder you've been single your whole life!

111
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,580
Yeah, single.

112
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,410
Well, you've never gotten married either.

113
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:51,420
That's because I didn't want to!

114
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,820
Even if I never get married,
I'd never marry you!

115
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,740
What's that supposed to mean?

116
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,140
Shawn!

117
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,060
Why are you wandering around like that?

118
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,460
I'm trying to find the feel of the wind.

119
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:15,900
The feel of the wind?

120
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:18,780
Looks more like you've lost your mind.

121
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,700
Everyone else is using this time to practice.

122
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:22,620
Tryouts are the day after tomorrow!

123
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:24,060
Exactly.

124
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:25,500
Look.

125
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:31,260
What's the big deal? It's just a tree.

126
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,180
What's that got to do with Yo-Yos?

127
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,620
Ugh!

128
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,540
How do you guys still not get it?

129
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,380
You just don't have the instinct for this.

130
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:43,260
Forget it. I can't explain this to you.

131
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:45,730
Crazy. Totally.

132
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:52,380
At the tryouts, once I bust out my Signature Move...

133
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,780
I'm gonna be an Instant Star.

134
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:56,700
Take care!

135
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,500
Signature Move?

136
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:10,140
Riding in your car...

137
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,540
is more exhausting than walking.

138
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:13,980
Mark my words Tony,

139
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:17,340
This time, you're definitely gonna lose.

140
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,140
You've never beaten me. Not once.

141
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,060
What makes you so sure we'll lose?

142
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:25,500
Why?

143
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,380
Your Jianghai Team has no training facilities...

144
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,260
no funding, not even Team uniforms.

145
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,180
That's the truth, isn't it?

146
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,500
Wow

147
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,060
How does she know all that?

148
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,900
Don't tell me the Principal is her mole.

149
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:44,220
That's not really a big deal.

150
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,580
It's not a big deal?

151
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:49,980
Stop pretending you've got this covered.

152
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:51,420
Listen to me.

153
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:53,340
For this Tournament, our School—

154
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,260
Chengnan High has plenty of funding.

155
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:59,280
We don't just have Team Uniforms,
we've even got Special Competition Gear.

156
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:01,500
And more importantly...

157
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:02,940
Very soon now...

158
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,620
we're heading to the Falcon Camp for Intensive Training.

159
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,140
Plus, we have an awesome Coach and solid Teammates.

160
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,060
Those little lambs on your Jianghai Team...

161
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:13,980
don't stand a chance of Winning.

162
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:17,340
Don't get ahead of yourself.

163
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:35,580
But I have The Secret Yo-Yo Training Manual.

164
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,020
Even if they're lambs...

165
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,940
I can train them into hungry wolves.

166
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,780
From where I'm sitting,
you're the one who looks like a hungry wolf.

167
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,180
You're out here looking for Sponsors today, aren't you?

168
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,060
Well, I hope you find one.

169
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:49,980
Just don't let me see your Players...

170
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,380
showing up to compete in Camouflaged Uniforms.

171
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,140
See ya.

172
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:07,740
She's sharp. She guessed everything.

173
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,100
Marrying a woman like that...

174
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:14,460
that would be terrifying.

175
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,340
Did you know...

176
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,740
Coach picked Mark to be the Team Captain?

177
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,180
Really?

178
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,060
I was thinking, maybe we should

179
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,470
buy Mark a new Yo-Yo?

180
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,460
Yeah, good idea.

181
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:42,780
But I didn't bring any money.

182
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:48,350
I don't have enough either.

183
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:52,680
If only we hadn't bought so many meatballs just now...

184
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:57,660
Oh, wait!

185
00:14:57,780 --> 00:14:58,620
Meatball!

186
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:21,660
Have you seen Chuck?

187
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:22,620
Nope, not at all.

188
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,460
Aiya!

189
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,380
Oh, man...

190
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:45,660
Ah, man...

191
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,990
What? Mark's actually gonna let me join the Team?

192
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:56,930
Of course!

193
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:58,600
Fine, I'll pay.

194
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,020
Now that's more like it.

195
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:02,460
Let's go.

196
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,460
What if we can't find a Sky Raider?

197
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:11,580
They had tons of stock in the shop yesterday.

198
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:16,860
Shh, look!

199
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:18,780
Isn't that a Sky Raider?

200
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:24,540
Wow, talk about a lucky break!

201
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:28,380
Heh, the Universe is on our side today.

202
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:29,820
Same plan as always.

203
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:31,740
Chuck.

204
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,140
You're up first.

205
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,060
Why is it always me?

206
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:37,980
Don't you want to be on the Team or not?

207
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,420
But...

208
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:40,860
I've never bullied a little kid before.

209
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:44,220
How is this bullying him?

210
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:46,140
It's not a real match.

211
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,060
Do you think he's gonna just hand the Yo-Yo over?

212
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:50,270
After we win, worst case...

213
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,380
we'll just pay him for it.

214
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,300
I'll go talk to him first.

215
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,540
Hey there, little guy. You're pretty good with that Yo-Yo.

216
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:02,940
Really? But I just got...

217
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,860
my 1-star Technical Certification Card.

218
00:17:05,500 --> 00:17:06,500
Really?

219
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,700
That means you can do

220
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:09,860
the 5 Basic Tricks?

221
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:10,620
Yeah.

222
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:12,540
I can tell just by looking at you...

223
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,940
you're a natural-born Yo-Yo talent.

224
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:17,820
But if you want to become a true master...

225
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:19,260
you have to go up against the best.

226
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:23,100
I've always wanted to test myself against a real pro.

227
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,020
In that case, would you be interested...

228
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,940
in a little challenge against that older guy over there?

229
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,340
Do you guys know each other?

230
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,260
No! No, we don't!

231
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:33,780
But... I'm scared I can't beat him.

232
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:37,980
Well, if you're that scared, then forget it.

233
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,830
Just go back to playing with your snot-nosed little friends...

234
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:43,740
and pretending your Yo-Yo is a potato.

235
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:48,540
Such a natural Yo-Yo prodigy,

236
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:49,250
just letting it all go to waste.

237
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:51,900
Take care of yourself.

238
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:52,860
Bye.

239
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:55,260
So?

240
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,180
It's in the bag.

241
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:58,920
Then why isn't he coming over?

242
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:03,420
Just relax. You gotta give the guy a second to think.

243
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:06,780
Be patient. Just 10 seconds.

244
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:08,700
Wow, that confident, huh?

245
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,100
Alright, I'll keep track of the time for you.

246
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:18,780
5... 4... 3... 2... 1...

247
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:21,660
Ha! Can't pull it off, can you?

248
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,060
We're outta here.

249
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:26,940
Hey, big bro!

250
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:34,520
Hey, little man. You've made up your mind? Great!

251
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,510
That's the only way you'll become...

252
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:37,500
a real Yo-Yo Master.

253
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,420
Older brother, even though I know

254
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,790
you're working with them,

255
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:44,700
I'll still take you on.

256
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,280
So how about this? Whoever loses has to trade Yo-Yos.

257
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:50,460
No way! I just bought this!

258
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,820
Then how about this? I'll go up against you with this one.

259
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:57,660
My Sky Raider is the latest model! No deal!

260
00:18:57,900 --> 00:18:59,100
Wait!

261
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:00,060
Hey, kid.

262
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,460
This isn't just any Nuclear Fission.

263
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:03,900
It's the brand-new Second Generation.

264
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:07,260
Wait... is that the Super Nuclear Fission?

265
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,140
Yep, that's exactly what they call it.
Super Nuclear Fission.

266
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:13,500
It's the best, newest Yo-Yo on the market right now.

267
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:16,380
Your Sky Raider is new and all...

268
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:20,700
but compared to the Super Nuclear Fission,

269
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:21,780
it just falls a little short.

270
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:23,100
Really?

271
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:25,980
Alright, here's the deal.

272
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:28,560
We can't be bullying a little kid.

273
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,260
If you lose,

274
